{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J48esuHZvzFf1qyR3drupG","type":"tool_result","content":"122:`mon→intohom`{.AgdaFunction} and `epi→ontohom`{.AgdaFunction} regroup the same\n123-data the other way, as a `hom`{.AgdaFunction} paired with the injectivity or the\n124-surjectivity of its underlying map.  That regrouping earns a name because the two\n125-resulting types are, by definition, `_IsSubalgebraOf_`{.AgdaFunction} of\n126-[Setoid.Subalgebras.Basic][] and `_IsHomImageOf_`{.AgdaFunction} of\n127-[Setoid.Homomorphisms.HomomorphicImages][]; so these are the functions that turn a\n128:monomorphism into a subalgebra and an epimorphism into a homomorphic image.\n129-\n130-```agda\n131-  record IsMon (h : 𝔻[ 𝑨 ] ⟶ 𝔻[ 𝑩 ]) : Type (𝓞 ⊔ 𝓥 ⊔ α ⊔ ρᵃ ⊔ β ⊔ ρᵇ) where\n132-    field\n133-      isHom : IsHom h\n134-      isInjective : IsInjective h\n135-\n136-    HomReduct : hom\n137-    HomReduct = h , isHom\n138-\n139:  mon : Type (𝓞 ⊔ 𝓥 ⊔ α ⊔ ρᵃ ⊔ β ⊔ ρᵇ)\n140-  mon = Σ (𝔻[ 𝑨 ] ⟶ 𝔻[ 𝑩 ]) IsMon\n141-\n142-  mon→hom : mon → hom\n143-  mon→hom h = IsMon.HomReduct (proj₂ h)\n144-\n145-  record IsEpi (h : 𝔻[ 𝑨 ] ⟶ 𝔻[ 𝑩 ]) : Type (𝓞 ⊔ 𝓥 ⊔ α ⊔ ρᵃ ⊔ β ⊔ ρᵇ) where\n146-    field\n147-      isHom : IsHom h\n148-      isSurjective : IsSurjective h\n149-\n150-    HomReduct : hom\n151-    HomReduct = h , isHom\n152-\n153-  epi : Type (𝓞 ⊔ 𝓥 ⊔ α ⊔ ρᵃ ⊔ β ⊔ ρᵇ)\n154-  epi = Σ (𝔻[ 𝑨 ] ⟶ 𝔻[ 𝑩 ]) IsEpi\n155-\n156-  epi→hom : epi → hom\n157-  epi→hom h = IsEpi.HomReduct (proj₂ h)\n158-\n159-module _ {𝑆 : Signature 𝓞 𝓥} (𝑨 : Algebra {𝑆 = 𝑆} α ρᵃ)(𝑩 : Algebra β ρᵇ) where\n160-  open IsEpi\n161-  open IsMon\n162-\n163:  mon→intohom : mon 𝑨 𝑩 → Σ[ h ∈ hom 𝑨 𝑩 ] IsInjective (proj₁ h)\n164:  mon→intohom (hh , hhM) = (hh , isHom hhM) , isInjective hhM\n165-\n166-  epi→ontohom : epi 𝑨 𝑩 → Σ[ h ∈ hom 𝑨 𝑩 ] IsSurjective (proj₁ h)\n167-  epi→ontohom (hh , hhE) = (hh , isHom hhE) , isSurjective hhE\n168-```\n169-\n170-Finally, we define the identity homomorphism for 